3d:["$","$L32","/services/structured-data/",{"as":"li","index":15,"className":"Sections_numberedItem__zJzfX","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedLink__gg0WT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedIndex__uRgOj","children":"16"}],["$","$L12",null,{"href":"/services/structured-data/","className":"Sections_numberedTitle__hoVr2","children":"Structured Data Implementation"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedDescription__wBeG3","children":"Schema.org markup as a connected entity graph — defined once, referenced across templates, validated continuously."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedArrow__E7xJy","aria-hidden":"true","children":"→"}],null]}]}]
3e:["$","$L32","/services/site-architecture/",{"as":"li","index":16,"className":"Sections_numberedItem__zJzfX","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedLink__gg0WT","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedIndex__uRgOj","children":"17"}],["$","$L12",null,{"href":"/services/site-architecture/","className":"Sections_numberedTitle__hoVr2","children":"Site Architecture"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedDescription__wBeG3","children":"Structure, hierarchy, URL design and internal linking. Why architecture decides discoverability before any content is written."}],["$","span",null,{"className":"Sections_numberedArrow__E7xJy","aria-hidden":"true","children":"→"}],null]}]}]
40:["$","li","Generative answers reward an unambiguous entity, checkable claims, and content a model can attribute with confidence.",{"className":"ProseSections_point__dPDSv","children":"Generative answers reward an unambiguous entity, checkable claims, and content a model can attribute with confidence."}]
41:["$","li","Machine readability sits underneath all of it: server-rendered HTML, structured data anchored to one entity, deliberate crawler access.",{"className":"ProseSections_point__dPDSv","children":"Machine readability sits underneath all of it: server-rendered HTML, structured data anchored to one entity, deliberate crawler access."}]
42:["$","li","Post-click experience decides whether the visibility you win converts into anything — being found is not being chosen.",{"className":"ProseSections_point__dPDSv","children":"Post-click experience decides whether the visibility you win converts into anything — being found is not being chosen."}]
43:["$","$L3f","Where visibility programmes usually go wrong",{"as":"section","delay":60,"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"ProseSections_heading__uxEsC","children":"Where visibility programmes usually go wrong"}],[["$","p","The most common failure is sequencing. Content i",{"className":"ProseSections_paragraph__Bhwli","children":"The most common failure is sequencing. Content is commissioned before the technical constraints capping the site have been found, so good work is published onto pages that cannot be crawled properly, and the programme reports activity rather than movement."}],["$","p","The second is entity ambiguity. If a business ap",{"className":"ProseSections_paragraph__Bhwli","children":"The second is entity ambiguity. If a business appears under three slightly different names, with inconsistent details across its own site, its profiles and third-party directories, a language model has no confident thing to attribute a claim to. It will reach for a competitor it can identify cleanly instead. This is invisible in a rankings report and decisive in a generated answer."}],["$","p","The third is measuring only what is easy. Rankin",{"className":"ProseSections_paragraph__Bhwli","children":"The third is measuring only what is easy. Rankings and sessions are available in every tool. Whether you are being cited, and for which questions, is not — it has to be established deliberately, by running a fixed set of prompts against the major systems and recording what comes back."}]],null]}]
44:["$","$L3f","How we approach it",{"as":"section","delay":60,"children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"ProseSections_heading__uxEsC","children":"How we approach it"}],[["$","p","We start by establishing a baseline that covers ",{"className":"ProseSections_paragraph__Bhwli","children":"We start by establishing a baseline that covers all five surfaces, not one. That means a crawl and index audit, an entity audit across the properties that describe your business, and a fixed prompt set run against the major AI systems so there is a real record of where you are named today and where you are not."}],["$","p","Structural work comes before content work, becau",{"className":"ProseSections_paragraph__Bhwli","children":"Structural work comes before content work, because the structural constraints are what cap everything else. Only once a site can be crawled, rendered and understood does producing more of it become worth the money."}],["$","p","Reporting keeps rankings, citations and enquirie",{"className":"ProseSections_paragraph__Bhwli","children":"Reporting keeps rankings, citations and enquiries in the same view. Rankings alone will tell you a flattering story in a year when clicks are falling industry-wide; enquiries alone will not tell you why. Read together, they say which surface is working and which needs attention."}]],null]}]
